    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0743" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811B.01/496: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-06T17:00:00-04:00">November 6, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2383. Your 3207, November 2, 2 p.m. The Department wishes you without delay to
                    approach the Spanish Government for certain concessions, either in a personal
                    conversation with Count Jordana or, <pb facs="0744" n="732" xml:id="pg732"/> if
                    you deem it preferable, in a conversation your Counselor may have with an
                    appropriate high official of the Spanish Government. Among the particular
                    concessions desired at this time are those set forth in the immediately
                    following telegram no. 2384.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d660-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
